  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Face Is the Screen",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Face Is the Screen\"**\n\nThe watch's own face leads. One real face picture, big and round inside a hairline bezel of 60 ticks, sits on near-black, and everything else stays quiet beneath it. The world is an instrument: a dark field with a faint dot grid, hairline rules, one ink white, and one red that appears only where something would be lost. It is futuretech and minimal, and it never glows.\n\nDensity is low and text is sparse. A screen carries a wide, light Archivo title top left, a few tracked capital labels, figures set like readouts, and one white button. The platform's own face carries body text, so the app reads native on iPhone and on Android while the titles, names and figures carry the identity. The coloured element on any screen is usually the user's own watch face. The interface itself has no colour beyond ink, greys and the risk red.\n\nRejected and not part of this world: a violet palette, glow or neon, and a 3D watch model or product render above a settings list.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Near-black field (void) under a 16 px dot grid of 6% white dots.",
      "One ink white for text, live state and progress; greys for quieter text; no second accent.",
      "Red only for what a reset would lose and for refusals.",
      "Hairlines at 18% ink; nearly square corners (3 px controls, 6 px containers).",
      "Archivo, wide and light, for titles, names and figures; tracked 11 px capitals for labels.",
      "The bezel: 60 ticks that turn, light up as progress, and spin once when a job is done.",
      "Exponential ease-out from 280 to 420 ms, and Reduce Motion honoured everywhere."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Ink Rule",
        "body": "Text, icons, live state and progress are all ink or its greys. There is no brand accent, no glow and no neon; the colour on screen belongs to the user's watch faces.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Means Loss Rule",
        "body": "Red marks only what a reset would destroy and things the app or watch refuses. Never use it for emphasis, decoration, branding or a generic error tint.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The 18 Percent Rule",
        "body": "A hairline is ink at 18%. The 8% faint hairline is reserved for scroll-under bar borders, the bezel's inner ring and secondary picture rings; it is not a quieter divider.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Engraved Title Rule",
        "body": "Titles, names and figures use Archivo wide and light. Never use a tall condensed or bold display style.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tracked Capitals Rule",
        "body": "Labels and buttons are small tracked capitals; running text stays in sentence case in the platform face.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Text Size Rule",
        "body": "Every style follows the user's text size. Titles and bar controls are capped at 1.5x, and labels may wrap to two lines rather than clip.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Interface Rule",
        "body": "Controls, rows, sheets and menus never cast shadows; they are separated by tone and an 18% hairline. Depth belongs to the watch face alone.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** set every screen on void with the 16 px dot grid, and let the user's face pictures be the colour.",
      "**Do** give a screen exactly one filled ink button; make every other action outlined, and destructive actions outlined in red.",
      "**Do** use red only for what a reset would lose and for refusals.",
      "**Do** draw hairlines at 18% ink; keep 8% for scroll-under bar borders, the bezel's inner ring and secondary picture rings.",
      "**Do** set titles, names and figures in Archivo wide and light, figures with tabular digits, and labels in 11 px tracked capitals.",
      "**Do** show progress as lit bezel ticks, either on the FaceDisc or as a Tick Bar.",
      "**Do** label demo data with the DEMO badge.",
      "**Do** animate with the exponential ease-out over 280 to 420 ms and give every motion a Reduce Motion path.",
      "**Do** cap content at 720 dp on tablets and let titles grow with text size up to 1.5x."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** introduce a second accent colour, a violet palette, glow or neon.",
      "**Don't** put a 3D watch model or product render where the user's real face picture belongs.",
      "**Don't** fill a selected segment, chip or tab with white; white belongs to the one primary button.",
      "**Don't** cast shadows from controls, rows or sheets; only the FaceDisc has depth.",
      "**Don't** round corners beyond 3 px on controls or 6 px on containers.",
      "**Don't** use a tall condensed or bold display style for titles.",
      "**Don't** set any text below 11 px or any text colour quieter than faint ink.",
      "**Don't** use icon fonts or emoji glyphs; draw icons as 1.7-stroke line paths on the 24 grid."
    ]
  }
